 # Privacy policy
 
 This is a translation. The [German version](/datenschutz) is authoritative.
-Last updated: 14 November 2026
+Last updated: 15 November 2026
 
 This page explains which personal data Snacklist processes, why, on what legal basis, who receives it and what rights you have. Snacklist is a shopping-list app for households on iPhone, Android and in the browser (app.snacklist.app), with the website snacklist.app.
 
@@ -57,7 +57,7 @@ Legal basis: Art. 6(1)(b) GDPR (performance of the user agreement).
 
 ## 5. Shopping list and household
 
-You can be a member of several households. We store what you enter in Snacklist: the household name, who you shop with (the kind of household: partner, family, flat share, club or team, just me or other) if you say so during setup or later, members, their roles and when they joined, invitations, lists (name, order, who created them and when), items (item name, quantity, list, who added and bought it, timestamps), a change history (which item was changed, by whom, whether it was added, ticked off, restored, edited or deleted, and when), and what Snacklist learns for your household (categories, stores, brands). What you type yourself under "Other" stays on your device and is not stored on our servers. A household can have several lists. If a member deletes a list, we delete its items with it. All members of a household see its lists and the other members' display names and roles. The app does not currently show the change history on any screen (the "History" tab shows your trips, see above), but the members of the household can access it. We use it for suggestions, and the changes you made are included in your account data export. The members of a household don't see which other households you are in. You choose one of your households as your default; until you choose another, it is your first household. Siri, Alexa and AI assistants work in your default household (section 7).
+You can be a member of several households. We store what you enter in Snacklist: the household name, who you shop with (the kind of household: partner, family, flat share, club or team, just me or other) if you say so during setup or later, members, their roles and when they joined, invitations, lists (name, order, who created them and when), items (item name, quantity, list, who added and bought it, timestamps), a change history (which item was changed, by whom, whether it was added, ticked off, restored, edited or deleted, and when), and what Snacklist learns for your household (categories, stores, brands). What you type yourself under "Other" stays on your device and is not stored on our servers. A household can have several lists. If a member deletes a list, we delete its items with it. All members of a household see its lists and the other members' display names and roles. The app does not currently show the change history on any screen (the "History" tab shows your trips, see below), but the members of the household can access it. We use it for suggestions, and the changes you made are included in your account data export. The members of a household don't see which other households you are in. You choose one of your households as your default; until you choose another, it is your first household. Siri, Alexa and AI assistants work in your default household (section 7).
 
 Prices and trips: You can add a price to an item. We store it with the item, with unit, currency and time, but not who entered it, plus the household's currency (euro to start with). All members of the household see the prices, the list's total and the total per store. In the "History" tab you can log shopping trips; each store is its own trip. For each trip we store the store (with its name at that time), the day, a copy of the ticked items (name and quantity, no price) and who logged it. If you start a trip in the app, we also store its start, end, pauses and duration, who started it and, for each item, its name, quantity, store, whether it was planned and bought, the planned and the paid price, whether another member ticked it and who added it. All members of the household see the trips and can delete them; trips logged by hand can also be edited. Without Snacklist Premium the app shows the trips of the last 4 weeks and only a summary of started trips; older trips and the items stay stored and are visible with Premium. Whatever is on the list ends up in the history the same way, for example drugstore or pharmacy items; for stores whose name marks them as a pharmacy, the app does not suggest logging a trip and leaves their items out of started trips. We do not analyse trips and share them with no one but the members of the household. We keep prices on items until a member deletes the price or the item, and trips (for started trips, with their prices) until a member deletes them, in each case at most until the household is deleted.
 
